What I Learned from the Shopping Cart Program in C
Introduction

I learned how to create a simple Shopping Cart Program using the C programming language in Visual Studio Code (VS Code). 
This program helped me understand how to declare variables, take user input, display information, and calculate the total price of items.

Concepts I Learned

1. Use of Variables and Data Types

I learned how to use different data types in C to store different kinds of information.

char item – Used to store a character or a single letter representing an item.
float price – Used to store the price of an item, including decimal values.
int quantity – Used to store the number of items purchased.
char currency – Used to store a single character representing a currency symbol.
float total – Used to store the total cost of the items.

2. Taking User Input

I learned how to use fgets() to take input from the user. 
It can read a line of text, including spaces, which is useful when entering an item name.

3. Calculating the Total Price

I learned how to calculate the total cost of the shopping cart by multiplying the price of an item by its quantity.

Formula:

total = price * quantity;

Conclusion

By creating the Shopping Cart Program, I improved my understanding of basic C programming concepts, including variables, data types, user input, output functions, and arithmetic operations. 
This program helped me understand how programming can be used in real-life situations, such as calculating the total cost of shopping items.